 "stimulus_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"3\">\n  <li>Two rocks are launched straight up in the air. The height of Rock A is given by the function <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>, where <span data-math=\"f(t)=4+30t-16t^2\">f(t)=4+30t-16t^2</span>. The height of Rock B is given by <span data-math=\"g\">g</span>, where <span data-math=\"g(t)=5+20t-16t^2\">g(t)=5+20t-16t^2</span>. In both functions, <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> is time measured in seconds and height is measured in feet.</li>\n</ol><br>\n<p>The following is a graph of the functions. Use the graph to answer the questions a – c.</p>\n<img height=\"268\" src=\"exercises/media/415da9423cafbc33.jpg\" width=\"279\" alt=\"A graph plots height (feet) vs. time (seconds) for two objects. Curve f (orange) peaks at 18 feet at 1 second, lasting 2 seconds. Curve g (teal) peaks at 11 feet at 0.7 seconds, lasting 1.4 seconds.\">",
